## Verdict

The question Cycle 892 called the most valuable on the gravity side
turns out to have the best possible answer: the theorem everyone was
worried about needs no identification at all. The gauge break is a
property of the whole axiom-grounded barrier space — every admissible
barrier, every refused control, even the free walk — and the machinery
provably could have seen it fail. What the identification really
bought was always smaller: expulsion, which follows from mere
containment, already booked as supplied on the Gate-B ledger; and one
incidence table that does move with the choice. A conditionality that
blocked three shipped residual lists is now a footnote with a theorem
attached. Independent audit still required.
